tonomic overactivation, especially given your prior elevated cortisol, rising stress index, and the FKBP5/COMT background in your records. However, **irregular heartbeat + shortness of breath + chest pain** is a **red-flag combination**, so a non-anxiety cause still needs to be considered seriously.\n\n**Important safety note**\nIf you are having **chest pain, worsening shortness of breath, fainting, severe dizziness, or a sustained racing/irregular heartbeat right now**, you should seek **urgent emergency assessment immediately**.\n\n**Next step**\nBefore I bring this to the Doctor Agent for a more accurate diagnosis, do you want to upload your **HRV data**? That would help refine whether this looks more stress-driven versus a broader physiologic rhythm issue.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_057202a153273ebf0169ef6ebdae488191998ab6aeac18ede6\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":370,"output":300,"cacheRead":22016,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22686,"cost":{"input":0.000925,"output":0.0045000000000000005,"cacheRead":0.005503999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.010929000000000001}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1777299129506,"responseId":"resp_057202a153273ebf0169ef6eba78dc8191b011a2abc43e79a1"}}
