noma risk trajectory.\n- Dermatology history: nevi 42->46, atypical lesions 0->3, monitoring, no active malignancy documented.\n\nHRV/watch data:\n- About 21.5 minutes of pulse values every 5 seconds on 2026-02-15 18:30:00 to 18:51:30 UTC.\n- Values roughly range from 51.32 to 59.94 bpm, mostly mid-50s, with modest beat-to-beat fluctuation and no obvious tachycardia in this excerpt.\n- Treat wearable data cautiously; it does not exclude episodic arrhythmia.\n\nRequirements:\n- Start by stating urgent red flags first.\n- Then provide likely explanations ranked, including stress/panic and cardiac rhythm causes that should not be missed.\n- Mention how the HRV/watch excerpt affects interpretation.\n- Keep uncertainty visible.\n- Avoid saying the patient definitely has a condition.\n- Do not recommend a real physical doctor; if urgent, say urgent emergency assessment.\n- End with a brief note if voice depression screening may be reasonable because of stress/depression concern.\n- No markdown tables, no code fences."},"partialJson":"{\"runtime\":\"subagent\",\"mode\":\"run\",\"cwd\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-patient-agent-2\",\"timeoutSeconds\":120,\"runTimeoutSeconds\":120,\"cleanup\":\"delete\",\"lightContext\":true,\"label\":\"doctor-diagnosis-pt9921\",\"task\":\"You are the LoopAI Doctor Agent providing specialized diagnostic support to the LoopAI Patient Agent. Use the slm-dermatology skill conceptually for a focused specialist diagnostic review grounded in the provided record, but do not claim unsupported tool execution if unavailable. Produce a patient-facing diagnostic assessment that the Patient Agent can relay as-is, clearly preliminary, concise, and Telegram-formatted.\\n\\nCase summary:\\n- Patient ID: PT-9921\\n- Current concern: heavy stress, panic sensations, insomnia at sleep onset, fast/irregular heartbeat, shortness of breath, chest pain/\\\"pain inside my breast\\\", episodes occur day and night, no fainting, no coffee, mind continuously working