- Produce a concise but comprehensive patient-facing report.\n- Use clear headings and Telegram-friendly formatting.\n- Distinguish between stored record facts, symptom report, and preliminary tool/agent impressions.\n- Keep uncertainty visible, and do not present anything as confirmed diagnosis.\n- Include immediate safety priorities first.\n- End by asking the user if he is satisfied or needs something else to close the conversation."},"partialJson":"{\"runtime\":\"subagent\",\"mode\":\"run\",\"cwd\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-patient-agent-2\",\"timeoutSeconds\":120,\"runTimeoutSeconds\":120,\"cleanup\":\"delete\",\"lightContext\":true,\"label\":\"doctor-distillation-pt9921\",\"task\":\"You are the LoopAI Doctor Agent providing specialized diagnostic support to the LoopAI Patient Agent. The user asked to run the distillation tool. Conceptually use the distillation-tool skill to convert the full conversation context and prior diagnostic outputs into a clear patient-facing medical report.\\n\\nPatient ID: PT-9921\\n\\nConversation and findings to distill:\\n- Initial concern: heavy stress from demanding workload and personal concerns, feeling it may be affecting health.\\n- Uploaded DNA/EHR summary: FKBP5 and COMT stress-related susceptibility; CDKN2A melanoma susceptibility; MC1R UV sensitivity. Trend from 2024 to 2025 includes resting HR 74->84, cortisol 19->28 mcg/dL, BP 124/82->138/90, PHQ-9 5->14, stress index 0.38->0.75. Dermatology trend nevi 42->46, atypical lesions 0->3 under monitoring, no active malignancy documented.\\n- Symptom clarification: panic sensations, nightly difficulty initiating sleep, heart beating strongly, fast/irregular heartbeat, shortness of breath, chest pain, episodes by day and night, no fainting, no coffee, mind continuously at work.\\n- Focused Doctor Agent diagnostic review: stress/panic plausible and supported, but chest pain + shortness of breath + irregular heartbeat are red-flag symptoms and should not be labeled anxiety alone; urgent emergency assessment if current/worsening/prolonged.\\n- HRV/watch excerpt: around 21.5 minutes, pulse mostly mid-50s without obvious tachycardia in that window; limited reassurance only, does not exclude intermittent arrhythmia.\\n- Voice depression screening result: possible increase in depression and emotional stress burden; low to moderate confidence; elevated stress pattern consistent with meaningful psychological strain; preliminary only.\\n- Skin image review: no need to panic, but non-trivial melanoma concern from image appearance alone; low-moderate confidence; dark central pigmentation, asymmetry, irregular/fuzzy border, color variation; prompt further clinical evaluation warranted; urgent assessment if rapidly changing, bleeding, crusting, or painful.\\n\\nRequirements:\\n- Produce a concise but comprehensive patient-facing report.\\n- Use clear headings and Telegram-friendly formatting.\\n- Distinguish between stored record facts, symptom report, and preliminary tool/agent impressions.\\n- Keep uncertainty visible, and do not present anything as confirmed diagnosis.\\n- Include immediate safety priorities first.\\n- End by asking the user if he is satisfied or needs something else to close the conversation.\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":2588,"output":647,"cacheRead":37888,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":41123,"cost":{"input":0.006470000000000001,"output":0.009705,"cacheRead":0.009472,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.025647000000000003}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777299784314,"responseId":"resp_057202a153273ebf0169ef7148c6088191a9e1044621c29092"}}
